{title: Faith of Our Fathers}
{artist: Frederick Faber & Henri Hemy}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[G]Faith of our fathers, [C]living [G]still in [Em]spite of [C]dungeon, [D]fire, and [G]sword —
O how our hearts beat [C]high with [G]joy when[Em]e'er we [C]hear that [D]glorious [G]word!

Chorus
[G]Faith of our [D]fathers, [Em]holy [C]faith, [G]we will be [C]true to [D]thee till [G]death.

Verse 2
[G]Faith of our fathers, we will [C]strive To [G]win all [Em]nations unto Thee; And [C]through [D]the truth that [G]comes from God,
We all shall then be truly free. Faith [C]of our [G]fathers, holy faith! We will [C]be true to [D]thee till [G]death.

Verse 3
[G]Faith of our fathers, we will [C]love Both [G]friend and [Em]foe in all our [C]strife; [D]And preach Thee, [G]too, as love
knows how By kindly words and virtuous life. [C]Faith of our [G]fathers, holy faith! We will [C]be true to [D]thee [G]till death.
